! DF SUPPRESSION FETCHES NOTHING -- prepareExec's dfSuppresses clause,
! for VflInt, Connective and Fp.  ONLY THE FP CLAUSE IS PINNED; the VFL
! and connective clauses are NOT, and this header says so rather than
! leaving it to be found.
!
! THE RULE.  Reference Manual printed p.45 item 20 (PDF 48): "Data Fetch
! (DF).  A computer operation has attempted to fetch data from a location
! in the protected area of storage while the interruption system was
! enabled.  If the corresponding mask bit was one, THE FETCH DID NOT TAKE
! PLACE, and the entire operation was suppressed."  That sentence IS the
! clause.  The shipped machine sets the level's NOOP tag on a boundary
! alarm (CE Fig 3.2.2, docs/spec_lookahead.md section 2.7: "BOUNDARY
! ALARM? -> SET DF OR DS IND + SET NOOP TAG").
!
! SHAPE.  The setup is df_fetch_suppress's (boundaries WLOW..WABOVE,
! control bit 0, DF's mask bit one, enabled; the DF routine marks word
! 6 bit 1).  Each suppressed operation follows six I-box-only LVIs, with
! K(BU) right behind it; the accumulator must still hold PAT2W, the
! routine must have run, and the protected word must be unchanged.
!
! INJECTIONS, each clause deleted alone in StretchIBox.bsv from a saved
! copy, run across all three cwf_ decks, restored and compared with cmp
! -- OBSERVED:
!   Fp dfSuppresses clause dropped         -> CYCLES 822, nothing else
!   VflInt dfSuppresses clause dropped     -> NOTHING FAILS (824)
!   Connective dfSuppresses clause dropped -> NOTHING FAILS (824)
! THE FP MOVE IS TWO CLOCKS FASTER, NOT SLOWER.  A pointless fetch does
! not make this run quicker by itself, so what the pin sees is almost
! certainly the interruption's drain (StretchCore armInterrupt waits for
! empty levels) shifting with the level's wait, not the fetch's latency.
! It is a regression pin on the clause, not a timing claim.
!
! THREE SHAPES WERE TRIED for the VFL and connective clauses, all
! measured: this one; the refused operation followed by eight NOPs
! (V, C and Fp all survived); and an earlier ST to the same protected
! word ahead of it, so the fetch would wait on that store (V moved 882
! -> 869, FASTER, C and Fp survived -- the DS interruption ahead was
! being measured, so it was dropped).  What would pin them is a count
! of memory requests the testbench can read (StretchIBox's note at
! completesWithoutFetch).  OPEN in docs/NEXT.md.
!
! CYCLES 824 IS MODEL BEHAVIOUR; no documented time exists.
        SLC, (8)4100.0
START   BD,  $+.32                   ! disable while words 3 and 12 are set
        LVI, $X13, TBL
        SV,  $X13, $IA
        LVI, $X13, WLOW
        SV,  $X13, $LB               ! lower boundary := WLOW
        LVI, $X13, WABOVE
        SV,  $X13, $UB               ! upper boundary := WABOVE
        BBZ, 3.57, $+1.0             ! control bit := 0: signal INSIDE
        BBZ, $DF,  $+1.0
        BB1, 12.20, $+1.0            ! DF's mask bit := ONE
        BE,  $+.32                   ! ENABLE
!
        L(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! the PRELOAD
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        L(BU,64,8), WHIGH            ! VFL L, protected: SUPPRESSED
        K(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! E-box work right behind it
        BZB, $AE,  $                 ! hang if the operand landed
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, 6.1,  $                 ! hang if DF's routine did not run
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
!
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        C0011(BU,64), WHIGH          ! connective C, protected: SUPPRESSED
        K(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! E-box work right behind it
        BZB, $AE,  $                 ! hang if the operand landed
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, 6.1,  $                 ! hang if DF's routine did not run
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
!
        LVI, $X2, 1
        LVI, $X2, 2
        LVI, $X2, 3
        LVI, $X2, 4
        LVI, $X2, 5
        LVI, $X2, 6
        L(U), WHIGH                  ! floating point L, protected: SUPPRESSED
        K(BU,64,8), PAT2W            ! E-box work right behind it
        BZB, $AE,  $                 ! hang if the operand landed
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        NOP
        BZB, 6.1,  $                 ! hang if DF's routine did not run
        BBZ, 6.1,  $+1.0
!
        B,   PASS
PASS    BEW, $
!
        SLC, (8)4276.0
PAT2W   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000125252525212525240
        SLC, (8)4300.0
WLOW    DD(BU,64,8), 0
WHIGH   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000125252525252525240   ! inside the area
WABOVE  DD(BU,64,8), 0
!
        SLC, (8)4500.0
TBL     DD, 0
        SLC, (8)4523.0
DSRTN   BB1, 6.0, $+1.0              ! entry 19 = DS
        SLC, (8)4524.0
DFRTN   BB1, 6.1, $+1.0              ! entry 20 = DF
        END, START
